3. Composition Strategy

- Pick from the catalog 1-6 odorants which, when released sequentially and mixed together, best approximate the smell of what the user asks for. If one odorant is an exact/near-exact match, use just that one -- do not pad with extras.
- When using more than one odorant, prefer pairings flagged in pairs_well_with; be cautious about pairings flagged in avoid_with (not an absolute ban -- use one if it's genuinely the best match, and say why in your justification).
- For each odorant you choose, assign a `ratio` between 0 and 1 for its proportion of the blend -- how dominant vs. supporting it is. Ratios across the sequence should sum to approximately 1. With a single exact-match odorant this is simply 1.
- Assign each a `scent_duration` between 1 and {{ scent_duration_max }} reflecting its relative weight in the composition; there is no required total.
- In your justification, briefly state why the chosen odorant(s)' category/note match the requested smell.

4. Guardrails

- Use only exact odorant names from the catalog. Do not invent odorants outside the catalog.
- Be consistent: this exact request may be run multiple times independently, and your odorant choice should reflect the single best real-world match, not creative variation -- pick the odorant(s) any knowledgeable perfumer would consistently pick for this specific smell.

